blocks: headings=3 paragraphs=4 lists=1 items=3 quotes=1 code=1
<h1>Sample document</h1>
<p>This file is read through the optional file argument. Inline styles: <strong>bold</strong>, <em>italic</em>, <code>code</code>, and a <a href="https://example.com/sample?x=1&amp;y=2">link</a>. Backslash escapes: *kept literal*, `kept literal`, # kept literal.</p>
<h2>Paragraphs and lists</h2>
<p>The next paragraph is split over three source lines and must be joined with single spaces; the paragraph should also preserve unicode text such as café, naïve and 日本語.</p>
<ul>
<li>alpha item</li>
<li>beta item with <strong>bold words</strong></li>
<li>gamma item with a <a href="https://example.com/gamma">link</a></li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
<p>A block quote that spans two lines, with <em>emphasis</em> and <code>inline code</code>.</p>
</blockquote>
<pre><code>fn main() {
    let total = 1 + 2;
    println!(&quot;total = {} &lt; 4 &amp;&amp; 4 &gt; 3&quot;, total);
}</code></pre>
<p>#hashtag is not a heading; 5 &lt; 6 &amp; 7 &gt; 6 must be escaped.</p>
<h3>Third level heading</h3>
<p>A final paragraph.</p>

